From 98a7ed0ce2bb301bec56564cf3a766676a2f98f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:05:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] packetizer: take a block's discontinuity once

A block flagged as a discontinuity resets the packetizer before its data is
read. Once a picture is complete, what is left of the block is handed back
to the caller, who hands it in again for the next picture: the flag was
still on it, and reset the packetizer a second time, after the picture the
block had completed.

Where a seek lands on a block that holds the end of a key picture and the
beginning of the next picture (a small key picture in a program stream's
2 kB packets, as at the start of a stream that begins on a black picture),
the H.264 packetizer lost the recovery the key picture gave and dropped
every picture to the next key picture; the HEVC packetizer its complete
sequence start, likewise; the MPEG video packetizer the beginning of the
next picture. The window attaching to a playing stream seeks so: an H.264
program stream showed nothing for its first group of pictures.

Clear the flag once the packetizer is reset.
---
 modules/packetizer/packetizer_helper.h | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/packetizer/packetizer_helper.h b/modules/packetizer/packetizer_helper.h
index 42b881b..db0741e 100644
--- a/modules/packetizer/packetizer_helper.h
+++ b/modules/packetizer/packetizer_helper.h
@@ -130,6 +130,14 @@ static block_t *packetizer_PacketizeBlock( packetizer_t *p_pack, block_t **pp_bl
             block_Release( p_block );
             return NULL;
         }
+        /* The discontinuity is taken. What is left of a block that completes
+         * a picture is handed back to the caller, who hands it in again: with
+         * the flag still on it, the block that begins the next picture too
+         * reset the packetizer a second time, after that picture. A key
+         * picture so lost the recovery it gave, and every picture to the next
+         * key picture was dropped (H.264, HEVC), or the beginning of the next
+         * picture was (MPEG video). */
+        p_block->i_flags &= ~BLOCK_FLAG_DISCONTINUITY;
     }
 
     if( p_block )
